# Cloudflare Pages security headers (applied to every response).
#
# One CSP block, for /* — Pages joins duplicate headers with a comma and
# comma-joined policies are enforced as their INTERSECTION, so a second block
# meant to loosen one page tightens the whole site instead (DS §12).
#
# The two third-party origins are both sanctioned exceptions to §2's no-runtime-
# CDN rule: self-hosted Plausible (§8), and Turnstile + the house mailer Worker,
# which §7 and §6 require for the contact form on /support.
#   script-src  challenges.cloudflare.com  — the Turnstile widget script
#   frame-src   challenges.cloudflare.com  — the challenge iframe it opens
#   connect-src mailer.thompsonblack.us    — the /contact/<product> fetch(); this
#               is a connect-src concern, NOT form-action, which is a navigation
#               directive and does not apply to fetch() (§7).
# form-action stays 'none': the form has no action attribute and never navigates,
# so a submit that outruns its JS handler fails closed instead of leaking fields.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), interest-cohort=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://plausible.thompsonblack.us https://challenges.cloudflare.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self' data:; manifest-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://plausible.thompsonblack.us https://mailer.thompsonblack.us; frame-src https://challenges.cloudflare.com; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'
